-- title:
--   Regularity on the ∞-Igusa branch of X_H(q²M') for q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ for which some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((\mathsf{q}))$ equal to the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q}\to L$ of the function field $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}(q^2M',\ \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$, where $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A\to L$, acting on $K$ compatibly with the tower $A\to L\to K$, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of $\mathrm{jq}=\mathsf{q}^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNumQ}$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ consisting exactly of those $f$ for which there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f\cdot y=x$ in $L((\mathsf{q}))$ after coefficientwise passage to $L$. Write $B=\mathrm{chartAlgInf}\,A\,K\,j$ for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$. Then for every prime ideal $y$ of $B$ containing the image of $\varpi$, containing $j^{-1}$, and containing every $b\in B$ whose image in $K$ is a nonunit of $W_0$, and for every commutative ring $B_m$ that is a $B$-algebra realising the localisation of $B$ at $y$: $B_m$ is a regular local ring, and so is $B_m$ modulo the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$.
--
--   This is the regularity statement, at $q=3$, for the two-chart integral model of $X_H(q^2M')$ over $A$ at the cusp centres lying on the $\infty$-Igusa branch, i.e. at primes of the pole chart containing $\varpi$, $1/j$ and the centre of the Gauss valuation ring $W_0$ of $A$-integral $\mathsf{q}$-expansions: both the local ring and its special fibre are regular. It feeds the corresponding statement for points of the two-chart model outside the image of the finite chart, used in the construction of the semistable covering.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_isRegularLocalRing_fibre_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_of_forall_mem_nonunits_gauss_xH_of_isAlgebraic_of_eq_three.lean

